WEBVTT

NOTE Narration is displayed in the caption strip below the video by default.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.170
This fictional team knows how to draft.

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:10.414
That supports a judgment about drafting skill; it does not prove readiness to use customer information.

00:00:10.414 --> 00:00:13.584
Examine purpose, people, process, support and responsibility.

00:00:13.584 --> 00:00:19.923
For process, mark developing because the permitted-input rule is not yet usable to staff.

00:00:19.923 --> 00:00:23.998
Attach the supplied practice policy and the evidenced gap.

00:00:23.998 --> 00:00:28.526
For support, identify the missing example and human question route.

00:00:28.526 --> 00:00:33.959
If evidence is absent, mark unclear and name what must be checked.

00:00:33.959 --> 00:00:36.676
Do not add an invented score.

00:00:36.676 --> 00:00:43.920
One participant may need a readable alternative; record that need without treating attendance as task performance.

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:50.712
The next action is a short fictional input-selection demonstration with a reviewer and policy contact.

00:00:50.712 --> 00:00:55.693
In your own project, keep proposed commitments and unresolved permissions visible.
